From: Perceival <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: enable AP_VLAN interface mode for ipq5332

The 4-address/WDS infrastructure (sta_set_4addr op, per-sta TCL
metadata, 4-address frame notification, NULL/EAPOL frame handling)
is shared wifi7 code and already built for every chip, but only the
qcn9274 hw_params advertise NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN.  On a mixed-bus
single-wiphy group (IPQ5332 AHB + QCN9274 PCIe) the missing bit on
ipq5332 masks AP_VLAN for the whole wiphy, so hostapd cannot create
WDS station interfaces and 4-address clients associate but pass no
traffic.

Advertise AP_VLAN on ipq5332 like qcn9274 does.

Signed-off-by: Perceival <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -661,7 +661,8 @@ static const struct ath12k_hw_params ath
 
 		.interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) |
 				   BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) |
-				   BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT),
+				   BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT) |
+				   BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN),
 		.supports_monitor = true,
 
 		.idle_ps = false,
